  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Dependency rule — proposal ADR-001",
      "items": [
        "Controllers and infrastructure adapters depend inward on application contracts and domain rules. Each module owns its repositories.",
        "Integration uses public module services and immutable events. Never share JPA entities as transport or write another module repository. Links in this tree mean containment only."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Logical data, not physical tables",
      "items": [
        "Identity/access: Account, Session, Practice, Membership, Practitioner, Invitation, record-local PortalLink; DeviceRegistration is future.",
        "Care: Patient, PatientRecord, AvailabilityRule, AvailabilityException, Appointment, VisitPreparation, Consultation, ClinicalAssertion, SourceRevision, Measurement, LabResult.",
        "Content/operations: RecordDocument, ClinicalDocument, DocumentVersion, StatementCitation, ReviewEvent, Publication, PublicationSourceGrant, ProcessingTask, ExportArtifact, OutboxEvent, AuditEvent, IdempotencyReceipt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Shared integrity contract",
      "items": [
        "Global accounts do not make patient records global. Practice-owned rows carry practice_id; composite references and RLS reinforce current application authorization.",
        "One transaction commits domain state, required successful audit, idempotency outcome and outbox/job rows. Appointment state, encounter state, task state, review, freshness and publication stay separate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Frontend and tooling",
      "items": [
        "React features/routes use the generated OpenAPI client, practice/account-scoped query state and local form state. Resolve unsaved edits before switching practice; clear caches on logout/switch.",
        "Figma foundations govern tokens/components. Radix, TanStack Query, PDFBox and exact dependency locks are proposals/setup checks. ArchUnit or Spring Modulith is chosen in story 10.1."
      ]
    }
  ]
